\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Illustration of the adaptive perception radius mechanism. The vertical distance map is constructed on a cylindrical sector with a fixed number of cells ($17 \times 13$). A smaller radius (blue) provides higher spatial resolution for precise near-field sensing, while a larger radius (purple) extends the perception range at the cost of reduced resolution. The policy learns to dynamically adjust this radius based on the robot's locomotion state.\relax }}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
